{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.KnotOperatorLpSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.KnotOperatorLpSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearForm.Properties","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.knot_operator_lp_selection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.knot_operator_lp_selection","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L125-L151","doc":"**Knot-operator LP selection** (`prop:knot-operator-lp-selection`):\nunder a `KnotOperatorLPSelection` instance, every confinement target\n`n_T` admits an LP-optimal selection supported on a *unique* knot\noperator `oStar`.\n\n**Derived**, not projected: composes `strongDuality` (an optimum\n`x` exists) with `complementarySlackness` (that optimum's support is\na singleton `oStar`) to produce the packaged selection. Neither class\nfield is this theorem's conclusion.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:knot-operator-lp-selection","label":"prop:knot-operator-lp-selection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.complementarySlackness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.complementarySlackness","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L121-L121","doc":"**Complementary slackness + generic non-degeneracy** (Schrijver §7.4):\nany optimal selection `x` for `n_T` has its support `{o : x o ≠ 0}`\nequal to a single operator `oStar`. A genuine LP hypothesis about the\n*shape* of every optimum (not a bare `∃ oStar, True`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.strongDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.strongDuality","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L115-L115","doc":"**Strong duality** (Schrijver §7.2): every confinement target `n_T`\nadmits an LP-optimal (objective-maximal feasible) selection. A genuine\nLP hypothesis — its content is the existence of an optimum, not a bare\nnon-negative vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.frob_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.frob_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Non-degeneracy of the Frobenius form: `det G ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.frob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.frob","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The Frobenius bilinear form on `H` used to define the\nMarkov pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorLPSelection","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L82-L123","doc":"A `KnotOperatorLPSelection R H ops` instance records the LP/SDP-\nduality structure that selects one knot operator per confinement\nvia the Frobenius Gram-inverse.\n\nMathlib has no formal LP-duality theory, so the two genuinely\nLP-theoretic facts — strong duality and complementary slackness —\nare carried as content-bearing class *hypotheses* (each cited to\nSchrijver). The block's selection conclusion is then **derived** by\ncomposing them (`knot_operator_lp_selection`), not projected.\n\n- `frob` / `frob_nondegenerate`: the Frobenius pairing supplying\n  `G^{-1}` as the LP-dual basis transform.\n- `strongDuality` (Schrijver §7.2): every demand admits an\n  objective-maximal feasible selection.\n- `complementarySlackness` (Schrijver §7.4): at generic non-\n  degeneracy, any optimal selection is supported on a single\n  operator.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Optimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Optimal","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**LP-optimal** selection for demand `n_T`: feasible and objective-maximal\namong all feasible selections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Feasible","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L67-L71","doc":"**Feasible** selection for demand `n_T`: non-negative, and its supply\naction meets the required multiplicity on every channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.supplyAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.supplyAction","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L60-L65","doc":"Supply action of a selection `x` on NF-channel `i` (diagonal read of the\n4-index supply matrix): `Σ_o x(o)·S(o,i,i,i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.objective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.objective","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L55-L58","doc":"LP objective: total crossing energy `Σ_o e(o)·x(o)` of a selection `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.supply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.supply","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The supply matrix `S(o, (i,j)) = NF coefficient of basis\nelement `i` in `b_i · toH(o) · b_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.crossingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.crossingEnergy","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Crossing-energy weight of each operator, used as the LP\nobjective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.basisFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.basisFinite","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Basis","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The (finite) Frobenius-non-degenerate basis of `H`, e.g. the\nNF basis `{γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻}` for `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.toH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.toH","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Each operator's image in `H` (the braid word evaluated as a\nHecke element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.opFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.opFinite","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Op","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.Op","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The (finite) operator index set, e.g. `{T_{2,1}, T_{2,3}, T_{2,5}, …}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily.mk","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KnotOperatorFamily","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-operator-lp-selection.lean#L25-L49","doc":"An indexed family of knot operators acting on an `R`-algebra `H`,\ntogether with the supply data needed to formulate the LP for\noperator selection.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}